// `@meta(n)` — the value form. Refused, by name, by BOTH toolchains,
// which is the only thing about `@meta` the differential oracle can
// ever check: the feature is zen-only from its first working line
// (`docs/PLAN.md:218`), so no test of what it DOES can be read by the
// bootstrapper. `docs/design_meta.md` is the decomposition.
//
// THE COUNT IS THE POINT, and `.count` says so. This program used to
// draw TWO diagnostics for one mistake: `expr_kind` had no `Meta` arm,
// the node fell to `Ty.Unknown`, `.name` on the poison drew nothing,
// and `println` was then told "codegen does not lower this yet:
// `printing a value of this type`". A sema refusal stops the pipeline
// before `emit`, so the second sentence is gone.
//
// position: the `@meta` token, not the argument and not the statement.

Point = { x: i64, y: i64 }

main = (env: Env) Res<i32, AllocError> {
    p = Point(x: 1, y: 2);
    println("{}", @meta(p).name);
    Ok(0);
}

// OWED (design_meta.md §6.1): a must-fail for the META_STEPS budget. The
// counter was REMOVED 2026-08-24 (#768): three spends on a straight line
// could not reach zero, so the test had nothing to red. Write it the day
// the counter returns with a rule that can loop. Kept below the program so
// no asserted position moves.
